WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.350
And then,
we’ll have the camera here...

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.870
Then, with some nice green
from the trees in the back...

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:24.700
Okay then!

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.500
Then, Satoshi and Go...
Can you come over here, then?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.310
Sure!

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.500
Now then!
I’ll roll the cameras, then.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.810
Then... five seconds...
Three... Two...

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.960
Hello to all the viewers at home!

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.190
Today, I’m at the Sakuragi Institute
in Kuchiba City!

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.380
At this institute, we find a pair of research fellows,
or special lab assistants, who are just ten years old!

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.590
Let me introduce you.
These are Satoshi and Go.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.790
Hi!

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.170
Nice to meet you.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.810
Hey! Sarunori!

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.910
H-Hey! Hey!

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.550
S-Stop that!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.350
Satoshi and Go are in the middle of
being interviewed at Sakuragi Park.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:52.220
They’d make a “boink” over there,
then another “boink” over here!

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.230
But it was all because someone
had messed with the Digda’s home!

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.580
And “vwoosh,” we solved it!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.780
That sounds amazing!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.830
Here you have research fellows Satoshi and Go.
Let’s wish them the best in their future endeavors!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.250
Now, to finish up,
please tell us about your dreams!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.380
My dream’s to make it to the top
in the Pokémon World Championships,

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.830
beat the Supreme Champion,
Mr. Dande...

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.490
...and then,
become a Pokémon Master!

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.860
A Pokémon Master?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.260
My dream is to catch every Pokémon,
and reach Mew!

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.060
Every Pokémon?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.770
Come on over, everyone!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.580
Catching Pokémon
helps you understand them.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.880
If I understand every Pokémon,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.410
I can reach Mew,
who holds the genes of every Pokémon!

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.320
In any event, I hope you’ll both work hard
to achieve your dreams!

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.410
That’s all for today!

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.420
See ya!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.260
Then, cut! Okay then!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.810
Thank you!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.430
Jimeleon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.920
Jimeleon?!

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.100
Jimeleon? Isn’t that
the evolved form of Messon?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.710
Then does that mean
my Messon evolved?!

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.410
Correct!

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.710
I wish I could’ve seen it happen!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.940
Let’s go and see it!

00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.810
Yeah!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.810
Hey! Jimeleon!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.790
Where are you?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.450
Come out, Jimeleon!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.760
What a mess...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.570
Even as a Messon,
it loved to hide...

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.360
Then we’ll just have to look all around!

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.310
Aceburn might know where it’s hiding!

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.530
Aceburn!

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.860
Messon evolved into Jimeleon.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.150
Can you help us look?

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.650
Jimeleon!

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.130
Are you here?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.690
Jimeleon!

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.830
It hasn’t turned up,
even after all this searching...

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.160
What if it’s hurt, or...?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.610
Aceburn!

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.460
Did you find Jimeleon?!

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.540
Right, so it’s that way?

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:30.610
In there?

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.210
Hey, Jimeleon!
Come on out if you’re in there!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.580
Is it really there?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.650
Sarunori?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:41.100
H-Hold on!

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.340
I’ll go check, too.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.510
It’s really damp in here.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.290
There’s mud everywhere.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.560
What are these things?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.240
What was that?

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.460
Sarunori,
I said hold on!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.010
Jimeleon!

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.410
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.820
So this is where you were.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:41.700
I called and called and you didn’t show.
I was worried you were hurt.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.850
Isn’t it great?

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.290
You’ve evolved and now
you’re as big as <i>me!</i>

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.070
Wh-What are you doing?

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:58.680
Oh, that’s right.
You can shoot Water Gun from your hands now!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.100
Um, Sarunori!

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:16.320
C’mon. Satoshi and Koharu are waiting, too.
Come on out!

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.640
It’s not good for you to stay
in a dark and damp place like this.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.370
I’m trying to help you here.
Just come back out!

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.670
Hey! Go!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.550
Are you okay?

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.970
Jimeleon...

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.870
Aceburn?!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.940
Seems like Jimeleon
doesn’t want to leave.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:57.230
Jimeleon...
You want to be like that Inteleon, right?

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.040
You will be!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:06.120
I know how great you are!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.360
So let’s train together
and make that dream happen!

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:13.870
Well? How about
coming outside to do that?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.580
Aceburn, don’t force it!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:42.090
So this is Jimeleon?

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.430
Yeah! Isn’t it cool?

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:48.040
Yeah. But also a little bit...

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.720
Jimeleon?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.430
Go, over there!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.800
Jimeleon! Wait!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:27.260
Jimeleon!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:34.330
What? Jimeleon ran away
from the Institute?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.370
Yeah.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:42.460
We pulled it out of a cave, then it got
this sad look on its face and ran off somewhere.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.070
Is that so?

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:47.590
Kikuna, put Jimeleon’s Index entry
on the main monitor.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:48.630
Right away.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:53.190
Jimeleon. Water Lizard Pokémon.
Water type.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:57.190
It keeps enemies out of its territory
by laying traps everywhere.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.500
Highly intelligent
but also very lazy.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.940
Very lazy?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.570
In some cases, evolving can
completely change a Pokémon’s personality.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.530
That’s right... Back when Hibunny
evolved into Rabbifoot...

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.680
And then when Rabbifoot
evolved into Aceburn...

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:25.010
But I— and I bet Aceburn, too—
we only brought Jimeleon out to try to help it...

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:34.210
Go... If my Pokémon weren’t happy,
I’d do anything to cheer them up, or cheer them on.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.430
I think I’d do that, too.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:43.320
Hmm... Perhaps Jimeleon was secluding itself in its den
and that’s why it didn’t want to leave.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.320
Secluding itself?

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.440
But why?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:52.780
It’s possible it turned more wary,
and wanted a place to relax.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.450
Could also be
preparing for the future.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.790
Caterpie is a simple example.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.310
Caterpie evolve to Trancell
and shut themselves away in hard shells, right?

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:09.930
I think that’s part of the preparations
to evolve into Butterfree and fly off into the sky.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:15.250
Then does that mean Jimeleon’s in seclusion
to prepare for its next evolution?

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.340
We can’t say for sure.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:21.560
Is this a common Jimeleon trait,
or is it unique to your Jimeleon?

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:26.490
Either way, just as Trancell
have their own appeal,

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:30.080
Jimeleon must have
its own quirks, too.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:35.880
Finding their unique charms and publicizing them
is our job as researchers.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.190
Here’s what I think...

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:43.440
It’s a living creature.
Wouldn’t you say that fact alone is marvelous?

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:46.920
Go! Where are you going?!

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.170
I have to go
look for Jimeleon again!

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.590
I’ll go, too!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.750
Me, too!

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.180
It’s getting dark outside,
so be careful!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.720
Any luck?

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:06.970
No good, I couldn’t find it.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:11.580
If it stayed invisible,
it could be really difficult to find...

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:15.070
I get that...
I was hoping Wanpachi’s nose would help.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.040
The scent seemed to just
drop off after a while...

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:23.500
Gah... It’s already dinnertime...
Where could it be?

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:27.500
I’ll try looking this way.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.710
Satoshi, Koharu,
you head back without me.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.120
Huh?

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.030
Go!

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:32.470
Thanks for the help!

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.920
Why...?

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.320
We’ll stay with you.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:56.730
Trying to act all grown up...
You still haven’t changed.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.130
You might be right...

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.200
What is it, Go?

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.330
Huh...? Oh.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:11.300
I was wondering why Jimeleon was ignoring me.
I suppose it might have some reason for secluding itself...

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.340
But I wish I could understand
what that was.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:20.490
So I’ve just been asking myself
“Why? Why?”...

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.180
Why?

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.580
Why is it?
You can tell me.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.240
Go?

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:31.970
What is it?

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.460
Back then, I...

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.110
So maybe Jimeleon...

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.060
Go!

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:17.450
I’m sorry...
for forcing you out of there.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.760
I remembered something.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:26.460
When I was younger, I didn’t like playing
with the other kids, so I was always alone...

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.210
And then my teacher asked me...

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:36.380
Go... Why don’t you play
with everyone else?

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.950
If you won’t tell me,
I can’t know.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.770
You can tell me.
Why is it?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.970
I didn’t even know why myself...

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:59.660
So being asked “Why? Why?” over and over...
It just made me frustrated...

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:07.170
Even if I went home, my parents are usually at work,
and it’s hard to ask my grandma for advice...

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:11.170
So, with nobody to turn to,
I just gazed at the stars.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:18.350
And then I thought maybe you were
feeling the same way, and came up here...

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.850
I’m really glad I found you here!

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.020
It means you’re just like me.

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:29.250
I’ve been rethinking things.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.980
If you don’t understand something,
that’s fine.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:35.400
If you can’t answer right away,
that’s fine.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:39.740
So... Jimeleon,
whatever you want to do, it’s all fine.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:44.690
Stay in your den as long as you want
without worrying about me...

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:49.660
Then someday, when you <i>do</i> feel like
being around someone...

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.960
I... I’d be happy...
if you let me in.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.340
Huh? Why am I...?

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:05.170
Jimeleon...

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:12.770
I’ll be with you in spirit,
even when we’re apart!

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.750
Come on. Let’s go.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:32.660
The Director’ll be waiting.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.340
Yeah.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.580
Any luck?

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.300
It’s there. It came back!

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:17.560
That’s great!

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.530
Yeah!

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:21.440
Then let’s get going!
I’m starving!

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.420
Yeah.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.970
Everyone!
I’ll play with you later, okay?

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:32.350
You too, someday...

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:37.280
Neither too close,
nor too distant.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:41.940
Perhaps this compromise is another good way
for trainer and Pokémon to connect.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:51.580
Pikachu!

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.450
Utsubot!

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.160
Trancell!

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:53.960
Lugia!

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.750
Achamo!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:55.540
Morpeko!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.250
Koduck!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.130
Cleffy!

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:57.830
Eevee!

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:58.580
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.250
Teppouo!

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.170
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:00.880
Metagross!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:01.920
Subame!

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:02.590
Me...

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:03.840
Metamon!

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:20.610
Pikachu!

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:21.440
Usohachi!

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:22.150
Chicorita!

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:22.940
Tamatama!

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:23.690
Mamepato!

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:24.530
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:25.280
Lucario!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.070
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:26.860
Seadra!

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:27.490
Laplace!

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:28.320
Starmie!

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.120
Miniryu!

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.910
Windie!

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:30.620
Iwark!

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:31.450
Kucheat!

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:32.200
Togekiss!

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:32.950
Sleep!

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:33.700
Ptera!

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:34.540
Raikou!

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:35.290
U'u!

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:36.080
Wooloo!

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:36.870
Ruriri!

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:37.620
Leafia!

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:38.420
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:39.210
Abagoura!

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.000
Latias!

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:40.750
Spear!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:41.500
Agnome!

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:42.250
Muma!

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:43.340
Madatsubomi!

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:44.500
Mew!

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:09.630
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:10.900
Go!

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:14.120
Eevee!
Do you want to see Showers?

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:18.870
I want to learn about
Eevee’s evolutions, too!

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:21.080
What would you say
to entering the race?

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:24.370
The Kids Marine Athletics Race
being held tomorrow.

00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:24.920
That sounds fun!

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.680
Yeah, I’ll do it!

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:29.470
We can enter, too!

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:31.380
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:34.340
Challenge! The Pokémon Marine Athletics!!
